Reads / queries (3/3 ported):
  [x] useWebhookChannels
        store    : NotificationChannelsStore.webhookChannels() : StateFlow<Resource<List<NotificationChannel.Webhook>>>
        endpoint : GET /notifications  (web useNotificationChannels list; transport adds /api/v1)
        cache    : CacheDomain.Notifications, key="channels"  (web notificationKeys.channels)
        derived  : filterWebhookChannels() = list.filterIsInstance<Webhook>()  (web `kind === 'webhook'`,
                   order-preserving) applied to every Resource emission (cached/loading/fresh).
        emit     : cache -> network (Resource.Loading[cached] -> Resource.Success/Error), shared feed.
        SI       : channel config fields are non-unit strings/bools — round-trip verbatim, no conversion.
  [x] useWebhookSignaturePreview
        store    : NotificationChannelsStore.previewWebhookSignature(secret, body) : Result<WebhookSignaturePreviewResult>
        endpoint : POST /notifications/webhooks/preview-signature
        body     : { secret, body } — both fields always serialize (web JSON.stringify(body)).
        invalidates: NOTHING (web mutation has no onSuccess invalidate). Pure utility.
  [x] useInvalidateWebhookChannels
        store    : NotificationChannelsStore.invalidateWebhookChannels()
        action   : bumps the channel feed trigger -> re-collects cache->network (web invalidateQueries
                   notificationKeys.channels). No-op when the feed is unobserved.
Mutations / actions (1/1 ported):
  [x] useTestWebhookChannel
        store    : NotificationChannelsStore.testWebhookChannel(id, title?, message?) : Result<WebhookTestResult>
        endpoint : POST /notifications/{id}/webhook-test
        body     : webhookTestBody(title, message) — a key included ONLY when value != null AND
                   trim() != '' (web guard); VERBATIM untrimmed value sent; all-blank => NO body
                   (server defaults). Mirrors the web mutationFn attaching a body only when present.
        contract : endpoint answers HTTP 200 in every delivery outcome, so a non-2xx RECEIVER decodes
                   to a success Result with `success == false` (status_code/error populated), NOT a
                   request failure — verified by webhookTestReturnsStructuredResultOnReceiverFailure.
        invalidates: NOTHING (web mutation renders the result inline; no onSuccess invalidate).

